      "math_academy_id": "q-115627",
      "knowledge_point_id": "75fd35db-6b4e-5820-b6ac-925d24a0f117",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola with Vertex at the Origin Given a Graph",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14096038/assets/aa0f2e4a43fa365822840441147a7d902b2aba7d218e7f738c279c4687fd1317.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-2,3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-2,3),$ we can substitute $x=-2$ and $y=3$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {3}^{2} & =4p(-2) \\\\ 9 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{9}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{9}{8})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{9}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{9}{8}$ is negative.",
