      "problem": "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(12,8).$",
      "worked_solution": "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(12,8),$ we can substitute $x=12$ and $y=8$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {8}^{2} & =4p(12) \\\\ 64 & =48p \\\\ p & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{4}{3})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{16}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
