      "knowledge_point_id": "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola Given the Vertex and Another Point",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(5,1)$ and passes through the point $(-1,5).$",
      "worked_solution": "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(5,1),$ we substitute $h=5$ and $k=1$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-1,5),$ so we can substitute $x=-1$ and $y=5$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x-5) \\\\ (5-1)^{2} & =4p(-1-5) \\\\ 16 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x-5) \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{2}{3})(x-5) \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =-\\frac{8}{3}(x-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
